  "finalReply": "Done. Everything verifies — summarizing.\n\n**What was delivered**\n\n- **Installed R** (`r-base-core`, R 4.3.3) since it wasn't present.\n- **`/app/ars.R`** — modular ARS implementation after Gilks & Wild (1992), consistent snake_case functional style:\n  - `ars(n, dens, a, b, x0, dlogdens, ...)` — primary sampler. Accepts vectorized densities (`dnorm`, closures, expressions, formulas), aliases (`g`/`lb`/`ub`, …), extra args forwarded to the density (e.g. `mean`, `sd`), optional analytic log-derivative (else central-difference).\n  - Module functions: input validation, density coercion/evaluation, `check_vectorized`, numeric derivative, `check_log_concavity`, `compute_knots` / `piece_weight` / `compute_hull`, `sample_from_envelope`, `upper_hull` / `lower_hull`, abscissae initialization with tail bracketing.\n  - Squeezing + rejection tests per Gilks & Wild; evaluated points adapt the hull.\n- **Log-concavity checks**: non-increasing slopes, tangent dominance at init and after every hull update, knot containment, plus the classic `h(x*) > u(x*)` rejection-time check — violations abort with a `log-concave` error. Two real bugs caught this way during development (near-parallel tangents for exponential tails; zero-width pieces at the Laplace kink) were fixed by coincidence-first knots and dropping massless pieces.\n- **`test()`** — 18 formal tests, all printing `TEST_NAME: PASS/FAIL` with mean/sd statistics: normal, shifted normal, exponential, uniform, half-normal, Laplace moments + KS tests, 5 input-validation rejections, 3 non-log-concave detections (Cauchy, bimodal mixture, gamma shape<1), derivative accuracy, hull validity, vectorization contract, and a chi-square shape check proving samples track the target (not uniform noise). Result: **18/18 PASS**.\n- **Sample files**: `/app/normal_samples.txt` (n=5000, mean≈0.00, sd≈1.01) and `/app/exponential_samples.txt` (n=5000, mean≈0.96, sd≈0.97), regenerated by `test()`.\n- Extra probes confirmed: `g=`/`lb=`/`ub=` aliases, expression/formula inputs, analytic-derivative and `x0` paths, seed reproducibility, and mid-sampling detection of a tail kink that passes initialization.",
